KG42.register("clusters-8efaca6b094e175579d219d8",{"id":"03-bilateral_p2p::v142-d-K002","paper":"03-bilateral_p2p","label":"Contract fulfillment and energy balance by actor type in the real-time market","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K002","label":"Contract fulfillment and energy balance by actor type in the real-time market","market_meaning":"Conditional on existing forward contracts, real-time contracts, and actors' net demand or generation capacity, prosumers bear obligations to meet load and fulfill electricity sales, suppliers bear purchase-and-sale coverage obligations, and generators bear fulfillment obligations that include capacity limits. This cluster forms category-specific real-time feasibility rules at the level of contract quantities.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["activation"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"R003-C002, C003, and C004 apply to P, S, and G, respectively, retaining their respective conditions. Forward contracts enter the accounting as existing commitments in real-time fulfillment; these conditions are not transferred into independent balance rules for the forward market. The assembly scope is limited to the contractual obligations expressed symbolically in the original formulas.","assembly_status":"assembled","boundary_rationale":"The category-specific fulfillment rules have independent contract inputs, responsible actors, and feasibility obligations, and their limited scope can be expressed by a single chain. They provide support for real-time selection to the negotiation cluster, but their primary assignment remains separate; fulfillment conditions are not equated with a complete execution process.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Jointly represents general real-time fulfillment requirements and the contract-balance conditions applicable separately to the three actor categories, retaining the original variables, parameters, and all conditional branches."}],"connections":[],"object_mappings":[],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G001","category":"unverified_source","description":"The category-specific inequalities come from transcriptions of the finite-valued domains of utility that have not yet been independently reviewed. The normalization of net demand in terms of contract energy, capacity dimensions, and upper- and lower-bound notation have not received independent source confirmation; assembled denotes only a candidate assembly within the limited scope.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-T001","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-T002","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e04","v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g01-e25","v141-b-g01-e31","v141-b-g01-e32","v141-b-g01-e35","v141-b-g01-e36"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check Eqs. (7), (10), (12) and the symbol definitions to confirm inequality signs, actor scope, and the basis of correspondence between contract quantities and capacity; do not use case-study parameters to fill in unknown units of frozen objects."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G002","category":"upstream_missing","description":"R003 expresses fulfillment obligations and the contract feasible region, without specifying physical dispatch, delivery verification, or loss settlement. The source assigns within-interval balancing to a faster control layer and leaves losses to separate settlement; this cluster therefore cannot represent a complete physical delivery mechanism.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::V::execution.energy_trade","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e10","v141-b-g01-e12","v141-b-g01-e25","v141-b-g01-e32","v141-b-g01-e36"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Retain contract feasibility as the assembly boundary; if an extension to a complete delivery mechanism is needed, have the upstream stage separately add source-supported execution, control, and settlement rules. This extension gap does not change the independent meaning of the current category-specific contractual obligations."}]},"rule_refs":["03-bilateral_p2p::v141-c-R003"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-3a452a468ee069da"]});
